1
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:05,036
You just put your AirPods in your friend's case.

2
00:00:05,086 --> 00:00:06,111
Will they charge?

3
00:00:06,161 --> 00:00:08,261
First, how does charging even work?

4
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:12,985
Two tiny spring pins in each slot touch two gold dots on the stem.

5
00:00:13,035 --> 00:00:14,714
Magnets hold the bud down.

6
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:20,411
Power flows from the case battery, and a chip in the earbud decides how fast to fill it.

7
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,388
Your friend's case has the same pins in the same place.

8
00:00:24,438 --> 00:00:25,716
So yes, they charge.

9
00:00:25,766 --> 00:00:27,297
But your iPhone notices.

10
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:32,508
It pops up “Mismatched AirPods”, because your buds and case were set up as a pair.

11
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:38,738
Put them back in their own case, or set them up again after your friend removes them from Find My.

12
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:43,226
A different generation can fit perfectly, and still not work properly.

13
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:45,394
Follow InvisiTech for more.
